  {"lesson": 2, "about": "you (1), you (2), you (3+)", "text": "*When speaking Pawnee you use a different form for you when addressing one person, two people, or three or more people. In this book we will use (1), (2), or (3+) after the you to show how many people are referred to."},
  {"lesson": 20, "about": "the two conversations", "heading": "Useful Conversations", "text": "Here are two conversations which should be memorized and practiced by anyone who wants to be able to identify himself as a Pawnee speaker or encourage elders to speak Pawnee. Alternate phrases are in parentheses."}
